on checks, and Uvicorn messages. A status badge indicates the console's live status. Controls for freeing up ports and refreshing the server logs are included in the server card's terminal toolbar.\n\n\nThe CSS targets the `#screen-servers` element, setting its height to a viewport-relative value, hiding overflow, and initially hiding the element. The `.servers-dashboard-header` defines a header with layout, styling and shadow. The `.dashboard-header-title` provides layout attributes for the header's title.\n\n\nCSS styles are being defined for the dashboard header title, including font sizes, weights, colors, and margins. The \"active provider\" switcher container is configured for a flexible layout with visual cues like color and icons for the labels and pills.\n\nA responsive grid layout is being established for the server cards. The grid adjusts to single-column on smaller screens, ensuring readability across devices.\n\n\nA compact server card design is being developed. This card includes layout for server avatars, titles, and meta information such as port numbers. Active server cards will have distinct visual indicators like a colored border and background.\n\nThe server title group is organized to display the title and associated metadata in a clear, concise manner. Individual meta tags, such as port information, are styled for better visual distinction within the server card.\n\n\nA dedicated terminal container is being structured within each server card. This container will feature a toolbar for controlling its behavior. The terminal will occupy available space, with a minimum height to ensure usability.\n\nThe terminal toolbar will include a title and optional subtitle providing context. Actions like freeing up a port and refreshing the logs are planned. Visual styles are being applied to create a distinct and functional terminal interface.\n\n\nThe terminal's visual appearance is being defined with specific styles for badges, buttons, and overall body. Distinct styles differentiate live status indicators from other terminal controls. Action buttons, including a \"danger\" style, are being styled with hover effects to provide visual feedback to user interaction. The terminal body will take up available space and maintains a minimal height. The terminal element itself ensures complete use of the parent container space.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/desktop_app/templates/index.html","EndLine":1180,"StartLine":1008,"toolAction":"View existing AI servers CSS","toolSummary":"View lines 1008-1180 in index.html"}}]}
